## Approach

Extend the existing FCA engine to run at two levels: global (all symbols, MIN_SUPPORT=3) and per-component (each component's symbols, adaptive threshold). The engine stays mostly unchanged — the orchestration of multi-level FCA lives in `build_findings`. Convention and SymbolAttrs structs gain a `component_id` field; check() uses it to scope violation detection. Component conventions subsumed by a global convention (same implication, >= confidence) are dropped before storage.

This approach keeps the FcaEngine simple (it doesn't know about components) and puts the component-awareness in the orchestration layer and the check logic.

