## Steps

### Step 1: Migration — add component_id column

Create `migrations/0015_convention_component_id.sql`:

```sql
ALTER TABLE conventions ADD COLUMN component_id TEXT REFERENCES components(id);
```

NULL = global convention, non-null = scoped to that component. No index needed yet — the table is small.

### Step 2: Convention struct — add component_id

In `src/conventions/engine.rs`, add `component_id: Option<String>` to the `Convention` struct and update `compute_id` to include scope:

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub struct Convention {
    pub id: String,
    pub antecedent: Vec<String>,
    pub consequent: Vec<String>,
    pub support: usize,
    pub confidence: f64,
    pub component_id: Option<String>,
}

impl Convention {
    pub fn compute_id(antecedent: &[String], consequent: &[String], component_id: Option<&str>) -> String {
        let mut ante = antecedent.to_vec();
        ante.sort();
        let mut cons = consequent.to_vec();
        cons.sort();
        let input = match component_id {
            Some(cid) => format!("{}:{} -> {}", cid, ante.join(","), cons.join(",")),
            None => format!("{} -> {}", ante.join(","), cons.join(",")),
        };
        blake3::hash(input.as_bytes()).to_hex()[..16].to_string()
    }
}
```

Global convention IDs remain backward-compatible (None case hashes identically to the old format).

### Step 3: SymbolAttrs — add component_id

Add `component_id: Option<String>` to `SymbolAttrs`:

